# Build context hygiene — keep the image build fast and free of host-local noise.
/out/
/.git/
/.github/
.env
# Local env files NEVER enter the build context. `.env` was already excluded; `.env.local` was not,
# and web/Dockerfile does `COPY web web` — so a developer's untracked secrets (AUTH_SECRET, IdP client
# secrets) were being carried into the image build, and `next build` was quietly reading them. It also
# made the build unreproducible: it succeeded on a laptop that had the file and failed in CI, which is
# exactly how this was found.
.env.local
.env.*.local
*.swp
.DS_Store
*_test.go
/docs/
README.md
UPGRADING.md
# Node/Next host artifacts (the web image rebuilds these in-container; never ship host copies).
/web/node_modules/
/web/.next/
/clients/typescript/node_modules/
/clients/typescript/dist/
